Thanks in advance

u is a vector and finally you obtain de u_i for each company (a value close to 1)

You have log(y)= alpha+ beta*X -u + error   (+u or -u depends  if you want  efficiency less o more than 1)

My problem is how I can introduce u_i as a ramdom effect  with a exponential(lambda) prior distribution, and lambda with a exponential (xxx) hyperprior

As a hierarchical model:

log(y) ~ normal(alpha + x * beta - u, sigma)
u ~ exponential(lambda)
lambda ~ exponential(-log(0.875))
alpha  non-informative
beta    mom-informative

