In-Reply-To: <qBm1kdY1zLg.nU4Cd-ENAgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <qBm1kdY1zLg.nU4Cd-ENAgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/qBm1kdY1zLg/m/3AgWFClDBgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi and thanks for your email. The names used are case-sensitive, hence
'id' does not correspond to 'ID', which I guess you want, doing

fm.test <- y ~ x + f(ID, model = "iid")  + f(ID2, x, model = "iid")

lcs1 <- inla.make.lincombs (ID = diag(N), "(Intercept)" = rep (1, N))
lcs2 <- inla.make.lincombs (ID = diag(N), x = rep(1, N))

then its fine.

Best
H

